  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on their minimum probability (i.e., the lowest probability of achieving a non-zero outcome), and prefers the one with the higher minimum probability. In this case, Lottery B has a higher minimum probability (90%) than Lottery A (45%), so the reason would select B. The individual refers explicitly to the 90-10 split, which corresponds exactly to the minimum probability of Lottery B, and uses this as the decisive factor. The term 'Risikofaktor' (risk factor) aligns with interpreting the minimum probability as a measure of risk. The information considered (minimum probability) and the justification (favoring high probability of gain) match the decision reason. While the individual does not mention Lottery A’s probabilities or explicitly compare minimum probabilities, the focus on the 90% as a favorable risk factor strongly implies reliance on the minimum probability criterion.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
